2026-10-25T02:36:52.6353890Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6372030Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6373420Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6373920Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6374410Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6374680Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6375030Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6375170Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6375500Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6375660Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6375740Z If you would like to
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6375920Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6376080Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6376650Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-25T02:36:52.6377000Z   $ sh ./install-nix
